   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">CHARGES MAY APPLY _Re: Dockside Green _On 2012-05-01, at 3:24 PM, Beeby, Gale wrote:__From Gale Beeby for new in Homes story by Ellen Moorhouse._ _Photos from Ellen Moorhouse __Dockside-stream: West Victoria's Dockside Green, a mixed use development on reclaimed industrial land, has earned more points under the LEED green building standard than any other project in Canada. Among its many features is a naturalized stream and ponds of rainwater runoff and treated effluent from the project's own sewage plant. __Dockside-caffe-fantastico: A popular place at Dockside Green is the terrace overlooking the harbour, where people enjoy coffees and baked goods from Caffe Fantastico and fol epi organic bakery. Adjacent to this eating area is, astonishingly, the project's sewage plant. There was absolutely no odour.__&lt;dockside-stream.JPG&gt;&lt;dockside-caffe-fantastico.JPG&gt;</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">CHARGES MAY APPLY _Re: Dockside Green _On 2012-05-01, at 3:24 PM, Beeby, Gale wrote:__From Gale Beeby for new in Homes story by Ellen Moorhouse._ _Photos from Ellen Moorhouse __Dockside-stream: West Victoria's Dockside Green, a mixed use development on reclaimed industrial land, has earned more points under the LEED green building standard than any other project in Canada. Among its many features is a naturalized stream and ponds of rainwater runoff and treated effluent from the project's own sewage plant. __Dockside-caffe-fantastico: A popular place at Dockside Green is the terrace overlooking the harbour, where people enjoy coffees and baked goods from Caffe Fantastico and fol epi organic bakery. Adjacent to this eating area is, astonishingly, the project's sewage plant. There was absolutely no odour.__&lt;dockside-stream.JPG&gt;&lt;dockside-caffe-fantastico.JPG&gt;</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
